AUDIO: 'not know, settings, and its hidden features. If you just got A2 Pro, you will learn lots about camera settings and how to use different camera photo and video modes. Quick disclaimer, Insta'

[00:25] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: '360 provided this camera. I am finally happy to say that the warm weather is here. I\'m finally able to work outdoors once again. Let\'s get started with all those tutorials. The first thing I\'m'

[00:37] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'going to do when it comes to photo mode is to answer one question that is popping up quite a bit in the comments lately. Should you select 4x3 or 16x9 aspect ratio when it comes to photos?'

[00:50] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'The answer is simple. 16x9 is perfect for landscape photography. It has a wider field of view, so you can get more background in the shot to create longer images. 4x3 is great for portraits or'

[01:03] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'photos of objects and macro shots as it focuses more on the object than the background. What is the difference between JPEG, pure shot, and pure shot'

[01:15] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'plus RAW? And when can you enable HDR? JPEG is just standard compressed format that takes photos the simple way. Pure shot gives you more dynamic range. It'

[01:28] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'reduces noise. The images are more vibrant. It\'s perfect for low light conditions. Raw images are not processed. They have the most data so you can edit them on your own in'

[01:40] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'programs such as Lightroom. All these three formats are available in both 50 megapixel and 12.5 megapixels. But HDR is only available in 12.5 megapixels. You can see it right here.'

[01:56] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'When you select 50 megapixel, it is off. When you switch to 12.5 megapixels, it\'s on. When you select 50 megapixels, you\'re not going to get zoom option. You'

[02:08] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'can only take photos with one time zoom. If you select 12.5 megapixels, you can zoom two times without quality loss. If you are going to be taking some street'

[02:20] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'shots like these, you might want to try two new Leica color profiles as this camera has Leica summarate lens. You will get to it by swiping left on the screen and accessing color profiles. The'

[02:33] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'first one is Leica natural. It has low saturation and high contrast that is suitable for urban photography, architecture, and scenes with distinct'

[02:45] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'light and shadows. The second color profile is Leica vivid. This one is suitable for family still life and colorful scenes as it has high'

[02:57] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'saturation and brightness enhancing the warmth of a scene with rich colorful shots. There are two more settings I would like to explain as they can be confusing to some. The first one is'

[03:10] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'metering mode. There are two available matrix and face priority. Quite simply, if you film a person or yourself, select face priority. If you film scenery,'

[03:22] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'select matrix. If you find that the pictures are a bit too bright, especially in highlights and sky, you can bring the exposure value down a bit.'

